    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "My project was all about analyzing NYC Regents Exam performance from 2014-2017. I started by loading the data and quickly realized the 'Mean Score' column needed careful cleaning, specifically converting non-numeric 's' values to NaN. I did hit a snag where I accidentally dropped too much data, but I quickly corrected it by reloading the original dataset and then applying the cleaning more precisely. After that, I dove into calculating overall mean scores, comparing them to a specific school I chose, and visualizing the distribution of scores and the top-performing schools. Ultimately, my analysis helped me understand not only the general landscape of school performance but also highlighted the crucial importance of meticulous data cleaning for accurate insights.\n",
        "\n",
        "My analysis of the NYC Regents Exam data revealed an overall mean score of approximately 66 across all schools. When I focused on 'P.S. 034 Franklin D. Roosevelt', I found its mean score to be significantly higher, around 76.75, indicating a strong performance compared to the general average. The distribution of mean scores across all schools, as visualized in the histogram, provided a broader context, while identifying and plotting the top 10 schools by mean score highlighted the highest-achieving institutions in the dataset."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "w4cdnwk5xZfC"
      }
